# Folders under here are work in progress, so a folder without its own index
# still has to be browsable: that is how you reach a version subfolder that has
# no landing page of its own.
#
# The listing is rendered by dashboard/browse.php, which puts it inside the
# dashboard layout. Apache's own autoindex is off: it can be styled but not
# wrapped, because HeaderName and mod_autoindex disagree about who owns the
# markup, and the table quietly loses its class names as soon as a header file
# is involved.
Options -Indexes
DirectoryIndex index.php index.html index.htm /dashboard/browse.php

# The files that must never be served stay protected here too. Same rule as
# the root .htaccess and dashboard/browse.php: a compressed dump is still a
# dump, and the match ignores case.
<FilesMatch "(?i)(^\.|\.(env|sql|sqlite|sqlite3|sq3|db|db3|s3db|dump|pem|key|log|bak|md|markdown)(\.(gz|bz2|xz|zst|zip|7z|tar|tgz))?$|composer\.(json|lock)$)">
    Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

# Archives stay reachable from this Mac, never from the network (28/09/2026).
#
# A backup zip of a site is a dump by another name: the review found real ones
# under projects/ holding a .sql and a wp-config.php, served to anyone on the
# same wifi as soon as Apache is opened to the network. The rule above cannot
# see inside an archive, and matching names like "backup" would miss the next
# one.
#
# ⚠️ Only DENY, and only to non-local clients. A Require that grants, here,
# would replace the Require a project set for itself (lesson of 15/09): for
# requests from this Mac nothing is added, so a project's own rules stand.
<FilesMatch "(?i)\.(zip|tar|tgz|gz|bz2|xz|7z|rar|wpress)$">
    <If "! -R '127.0.0.0/8' && ! -R '::1'">
        Require all denied
    </If>
</FilesMatch>
